      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That's a fair point—when you're drained, the idea of \"creating meaning\" can feel like another task on an endless to-do list. But maybe the sandcastle isn't about the final product; it's about the way your hands feel in the sand, the rhythm of the work, or the brief satisfaction of a shape you like before the wave comes. You don't have to build a whole castle today—just a small, crooked tower, or even just sit and watch the tide. The effort only matters if it brings you a moment of peace, not because it has to last.",
